From 314f42cfc3543c873943ddae7bea93f347518aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] Locked windows keep their buttons clickable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Locked, a window let all of the mouse through but its scroll strip, so
none of its buttons could be reached: not History from the meter, not
Details' History button, not the plugin dock's tabs. Each page now tells
the backend where its buttons are (lockedButtons.js, set_locked_buttons),
and while the window is locked those rectangles stay in its input region
next to the lock button and the scroll strip; everywhere else clicks go
to the game. They follow the page: a menu that opens, the meter growing,
the window resized.

Kept clickable: the meter's header and footer buttons (not reset and the
capture switch, so a stray click can't end a fight's numbers), Details'
header and its settings menu, Battle History's header and filters, the
plugin dock's bar, tabs and panel bars, and plugins' bars. Settings →
Meter Settings → "Locked: buttons stay clickable", on unless turned off.
Not while a screenshot tool is in front. Linux; on Windows the lock is a
pointer watch and this does nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBQati3x8VviBbpY9juEWf
